      "locations": [
        {
          "label": "Miri CLI",
          "path": "{prefix}/bin/miri",
          "purpose": "Cargo-backed Miri run/test with the pinned precompiled sysroot"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Three executed deterministic fixture paths only; no all-input or Rust soundness proof. Tree Borrows is experimental. Runtime prefix is immutable; Cargo output and home are outside the prefix.",
        "Host Ubuntu 24.04 libc, libstdc++, zlib and libgcc ABI are required. The delivered profile uses dependency-free Cargo fixtures and includes no network setup or rustup install.",
        "The bin/miri convenience entrypoint accepts cargo-miri subcommands, for example miri run --offline --manifest-path PROJECT/Cargo.toml. Interpreter binary remains under runtime/bin/miri.",
        "Runtime is a SHA-locked compressed capsule. CPG0.21.14 SDK must be importable by python3. CLI/check verifies and expands the full runtime into a private writable build directory per invocation, then removes it; CPG_RUNTIME_BUILD can choose a location outside the immutable prefix. Functional logs and inputs are retained separately from the temporary runtime.",
        "The expanded capsule is additionally checked by the original SDK ELF/runtime checker against actual current_target; its private libraries must resolve inside that expansion. Undeclared ambient LD_* variables are excluded from qualified execution."
      ],
      "summary": "Paired Miri nightly with ready MIR sysroot for safe Rust and explicit UB diagnostics."
    },
